WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:02.490
- So wait, how did you end up
getting into acting though?

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:03.660
How did that happen?

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:07.860
- So strangely I got in through
sports, through basketball.

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:09.570
So that's been a passion of mine.

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:11.100
I grew up playing basketball.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:12.360
Actually, I played in high school,

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:13.920
got a scholarship, played in college.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:14.753
- [Kelly] Oh, wow.

00:00:14.753 --> 00:00:16.830
- And one day, a buddy of mine,

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:19.440
this kinda is gonna go
back to pre cell phones,

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:22.200
where people used to
yell out your window, yo!

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:23.520
Called me out the window, "Ramon!".

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:25.983
So I look out my window
and my boy is there,

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:28.740
Bobito Garcia, is a DJ as well.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:31.130
And he's like, "There's this Nike event.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:31.963
"Do you want to come?"

00:00:31.963 --> 00:00:33.720
And I was like, mm,
again, a little reluctant.

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:35.010
He's like, they're giving
away free sneakers.

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:35.939
I was like, I'm there, done.

00:00:35.939 --> 00:00:37.020
(audience laughing)

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:38.250
So I go to the event.

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.320
And I could do this one trick,

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:41.970
which was I could spin
a ball on my finger,

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:44.310
keep the ball spinning, put it on a pen,

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.851
put the spinning ball on the
pen in my mouth, no hands.

00:00:46.851 --> 00:00:48.060
- How did you learn to do that?

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:49.260
- The Harlem Globetrotters.

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:51.180
So I would watch them as a kid.

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:53.089
- No, everybody watches
them, but we can't do it!

00:00:53.089 --> 00:00:54.120
(audience laughing)

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.830
But I slept with my ball.

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:57.600
I named her, her name was Betsy.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:59.000
I mean, it was a thing like.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:00.720
- Oh, my gosh!
- You know?

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:03.030
What it did for me was
amazing, this round object.

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:05.370
For awhile I traveled around the world.

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:07.920
doing halftime shows and performances.

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:09.393
- So cool.
- Before acting.

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:11.453
Nike then was like, hey,

00:01:11.453 --> 00:01:12.990
come be a part of these commercials.

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:14.970
That's what put me in front of the camera.

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:16.655
- And you liked it.

00:01:16.655 --> 00:01:17.488
- I was like, I liked it.

00:01:17.488 --> 00:01:19.530
Yeah, it's funny how like
the dance, the basketball,

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:22.920
somehow all kinda incorporates
into a a bit of performance.

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:24.690
- Yeah, 'cause it's all
a form of performance,

00:01:24.690 --> 00:01:26.280
I guess, yeah.
- Exactly.

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:27.630
- Do you still know how to do the trick?

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:29.190
I'm challenging you.

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:30.090
- Maybe.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:31.290
- Okay.
- Do we have anything

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:32.123
so I can?
- Oh, it's so

00:01:32.123 --> 00:01:32.956
interesting, we do.

00:01:32.956 --> 00:01:34.400
- Oh, just by chance.
(audience laughing)

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:36.311
(audience cheering)
- Let's get the basketball!

00:01:36.311 --> 00:01:37.245
(audience applauding)

00:01:37.245 --> 00:01:39.779
And course, the Pilot G-2 pen,

00:01:39.779 --> 00:01:42.150
the go-to pen of the Kelly Clarkson Show.

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:44.400
Pilot loves celebrating
unstoppable people like Ramon.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:45.990
So, okay, let's see if you can teach me.

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:47.220
- Let's see, so here's this.

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:48.540
I'll start with this.
- Yes, no, you're up here.

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:49.373
You're gonna have to try too.

00:01:49.373 --> 00:01:50.220
- Come on up, absolutely.

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:51.390
- You're not getting outta this.

00:01:51.390 --> 00:01:52.273
Oh, my God!
- Oh, just?

00:01:52.273 --> 00:01:53.610
- [Audience] Oh!

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:54.443
- [Kelly] What?

00:01:54.443 --> 00:01:55.276
- All right, so here we go.

00:01:55.276 --> 00:01:57.581
Kelly, I need you to hold
this incredibly strong.

00:01:57.581 --> 00:01:58.414
(Kelly shrieking)

00:01:58.414 --> 00:01:59.580
And don't move.
- Incredibly strong.

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:00.413
- Don't move, just solid.

00:02:00.413 --> 00:02:01.246
Don't move.
- I'm very strong.

00:02:01.246 --> 00:02:02.220
I'm very strong.

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:03.102
- [Ramon] There you go.

00:02:03.102 --> 00:02:05.466
(audience cheering)
(audience applauding)

00:02:05.466 --> 00:02:06.299
- Ah!

00:02:06.299 --> 00:02:08.455
- You know what, I'm not
gonna leave you here alone.

00:02:08.455 --> 00:02:09.288
- Uh-oh.

00:02:11.073 --> 00:02:12.120
- You hold that.

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:13.862
- It's still happening.
(audience cheering)

00:02:13.862 --> 00:02:15.730
(Emma shrieking)

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:17.230
Ramon, oh my gosh!

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:21.350
- Wow.

00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:24.259
- Oh, now you're just
showing off, Ramon! (laughs)

00:02:24.259 --> 00:02:26.066
(audience cheering)
(audience applauding)

00:02:26.066 --> 00:02:27.182
That is incredible!

